.TH LIBMPQ__FILE_NUMBER_IDENTITY 3 2026-11-04 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__file_number_identity \- resolve an exact filename locale and platform
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>

int32_t libmpq__file_number_identity(
        mpq_archive_s *archive, const char *filename,
        uint16_t locale, uint16_t platform, uint32_t *file_number);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Select the exact stored classic locale/platform identity for filename.
There is no neutral fallback or global locale state. The existing ordinary
libmpq__file_number(3) behavior is unchanged. Conflicting or duplicate
identities return FORMAT rather than choosing the first hit.
.PP
HET/BET-only identities accept only (0, 0). A missing classic selector is
not satisfied by a name-only BET row when other classic variants exist.
A name found only through HET/BET remains unqualified, even if its payload
has classic aliases under other names. Reduced extended hashes cannot establish exact
identity and are rejected. Indexed metadata queries can use the result;
for encrypted reads use the exact named stream so the filename is supplied.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Return 0 on success or a negative libmpq error. A valid output is entirely
cleared on failure. No partial stream is returned.
.SH ERRORS
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST indicates missing required arguments, an absent identity
or the end of enumeration. LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT indicates malformed canonical
mappings, contradictory duplicate identities or unsupported reduced hashes.
Read-only identity queries reject writable archives with
LIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED. Stream opening rejects invalid writer handles
with LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST. Existing allocation, source I/O and decode errors
are propagated. All source archives remain unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__file_number (3),
.BR libmpq__file_variant (3),
.BR libmpq__stream_open_name_identity (3),
.BR libmpq__stream_close (3)
